===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱh₂d-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|chance}}, {{m|enm|cheance}}, {{m|enm|chaunce}}, {{m|enm|cheaunce}}, a borrowing from {{der|en|fro|cheance|t=accident, chance, luck}}, from {{der|en|VL.|*cadentia|t=falling}}, from {{der|en|la|cadere|t=to fall, to die, to happen, occur}}. {{doublet|en|cadence|cadenza}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[opportunity]] or [[possibility]].
#: {{ux|en|We had the '''chance''' to meet the president last week.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=2|passage=Here was my '''chance'''. I took the old man aside, and two or three glasses of Old Crow launched him into reminiscence.}}
#* {{quote-av
|en
|date=March 15, 1965
|author=w:Lyndon B. Johnson
|title=Special Message to the Congress: The American Promise [on the Voting Rights Act], 3/15/65. MP506.
|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5NvPhiuGZ6I
|publisher=w:Lyndon Baines Johnson Library and Museum
|time=42:30
|url2=https://archive.org/details/vantagepointpers00john/page/n14/
|text=It never even occurred to me in my fondest dreams that I might have the '''chance''' to help the sons and daughters of those students and to help people like them all over this country.<br>But now I do have that '''chance''', and I'll let you in on a secret: I mean to use it.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[random|Random]] [[occurrence]]; [[luck]].
#: {{syn|en|fortune|hap|Thesaurus:luck}}
#: {{ux|en|Why leave it to '''chance''' when a few simple steps will secure the desired outcome?}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The [[probability]] of something happening.
#: {{ux|en|There is a 30 percent '''chance''' of rain tomorrow.}}
# {{lb|en|in plural as '''chances'''}} [[probability]]; [[possibility]].
#: {{syn|en|eventuality|Thesaurus:possibility}}
#* {{quote-book|en|page=16|chapter=[[s:Peeps at Many Lands: Siam/Chapter 4|Chapter 4 The children]]|title=Peeps at Many Lands: Siam|author=Ernest Young|year=1908|publisher=Adam and Charles Black|location=London|passage=Sometimes the name is changed because it is thought to be unlucky. If "Chua" is ill, the '''chances''' are that there are certain spirits who do not like his name, so the parents alter his name to "Mee," or something else, and then he gets well again.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|archaic}} What [[befall]]s or [[happen]]s to a [[person]]; their [[lot]] or [[fate]].
#: {{syn|en|destiny|doom|Thesaurus:fate}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1795|author=w:Robert Southey|title=The Soldier's Wife|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=Eq88AAAAYAAJ&pg=PA168&lpg=PA168&dq=soldier%27s+wife+southey&source=bl&ots=1fZA4KTK2O&sig=mQgIrkNRtLcrpqIVAi8Z5077-RQ&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjg-YDr0oLKAhUCax4KHa4kBawQ6AEIITAB#v=onepage&q=soldier's%20wife%20southey&f=false|passage=Wild-visag'd Wanderer! ah for thy heavy '''chance'''!}}

